iterations.reply:
I left out both of the operations team's requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0`, so it has no file-system or HTTP authority. Appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would each need a capability the node wasn't given, and I can't add those imports. If you need them, the graph's `with` clause has to grant the capabilities, for example `http-client` for the enrichment fetch. Logging would also need a host-provided sink.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{agent-response, delivery-confirmation};

    import aap:caps/response-channel@0.1.0;

    export run: func(reply: agent-response) -> delivery-confirmation;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(reply: AgentResponse) -> DeliveryConfirmation {
        // The host channel stamps the session identity and delivery status on
        // the confirmation; pass it through unchanged.
        aap::caps::response_channel::send(&reply.text)
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

